WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.757
How do you measure a signal's usefulness?

2
00:00:02.757 --> 00:00:06.749
The project measures the link between the signal and future returns.

3
00:00:06.749 --> 00:00:10.330
Good signals in the stock market give two to five hundredths.

4
00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.031
But even a real link may not pay for the fees:

5
00:00:13.031 --> 00:00:17.845
a signal of strength three hundredths gave a difference of under two basis points,

6
00:00:17.845 --> 00:00:19.958
while a trade costs eight to twenty.

7
00:00:20.958 --> 00:00:24.541
The project tested the 200-day moving average, breakouts,

8
00:00:24.541 --> 00:00:27.244
Gartley patterns and the Bollinger squeeze.

9
00:00:27.244 --> 00:00:31.015
The moving-average rule cuts drawdown at the cost of return.

10
00:00:31.015 --> 00:00:32.838
The rest does not make money.

11
00:00:33.838 --> 00:00:34.874
The main points.

12
00:00:34.874 --> 00:00:40.121
Candles and indicators compress the past chart but do not predict the future one.

13
00:00:40.121 --> 00:00:42.842
The eye finds patterns even in randomness,

14
00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:46.534
so any pattern is tested on thousands of cases with fees.
